<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Manifold entitlements. Committed and version-controlled rather than XcodeGen's inline
    `entitlements:` key, so what the app is granted is reviewable in a diff.

    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation

    Hardened runtime normally requires every library a process loads to be signed by the SAME
    Team ID as the main executable (or by Apple). This entitlement lifts that requirement.
    THERE ARE THREE DISTINCT REASONS IT IS HERE, and losing track of any one of them would
    make removing it look safe when it is not:

      1. THE NDI RUNTIME IS dlopen'd.
         App/NDI/NDIBridge.mm loads /usr/local/lib/libndi.dylib at run time from the user's
         own NDI installation — the SDK's licence does not permit us to vendor it, so it is
         never linked and never bundled. It is signed by Vizrt NDI AB, not by us. Without
         this entitlement the dlopen fails in the SIGNED build only, and NDI discovery
         returns an empty source list with no error anywhere.

      2. THE DECKLINK API IS CFBundle-LOADED.
         /Library/Frameworks/DeckLinkAPI.framework is installed by Blackmagic's Desktop Video
         driver and signed by Blackmagic Design. Same failure shape: SDI output silently
         unavailable in a signed build.

      3. IT IS WHAT MAKES THE LGPL §6 RELINKING RIGHT EXERCISABLE.  <- added with the shared
         FFmpeg migration; the newest reason and the least obvious.
         Manifold ships FFmpeg as five dylibs in Contents/Frameworks specifically so a user
         can replace them with their own build (LGPL 2.1 section 6(b) — see
         ThirdParty/ffmpeg/README.md, and the FFmpeg entry in App/AboutWindow.swift which
         carries the instructions). A user's replacement dylib is, by definition, not signed
         by us: it will be ad-hoc signed at best. Without this entitlement hardened runtime
         would refuse to load it, and the right we are obliged to grant would exist on paper
         only — the app would ship in a section-6-shaped configuration that cannot actually
         be relinked.

    CONSEQUENCE, AND THE REASON ALL THREE ARE WRITTEN DOWN: REASONS 1 AND 2 COULD BOTH GO
    AWAY — NDI could be dropped, DeckLink could move to a linked framework — AND THIS
    ENTITLEMENT WOULD STILL BE REQUIRED, for reason 3, for as long as FFmpeg is linked at
    all. Do not remove it on the grounds that the dlopen/CFBundle cases no longer apply.

    scripts/release-mac.sh asserts this entitlement is present on the signed app and fails
    the release if it is missing.
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
